0.9.29-go.9 (unreleased):
    NEW:
    * Go backend: a DEFAULT on a BMPString or UniversalString member is
      accepted (a plain string in Go). Before, it was refused (exit 70).
    * Go backend: a DEFAULT on a UTF8String, GeneralString, GraphicString,
      TeletexString, T61String, VideotexString, ObjectDescriptor, UTCTime or
      GeneralizedTime member is accepted (a plain string in Go). Before, it
      was refused (exit 70) with a message that wrongly blamed character
      strings in general.
    FIXES:
    * C generator (also for plain C users): the DEFAULT of a BMPString or
      UniversalString member is stored as UCS-2 / UCS-4 big-endian ("hi" is
      00 68 00 69 and 00 00 00 68 00 00 00 69), converted from the UTF-8
      literal in the specification. Before, it was stored one byte per
      character, so a decoder filled an absent member with the wrong value
      and the encoder never omitted a correct one. A character that does not
      fit (above U+FFFF for BMPString) or invalid UTF-8 now stops generation
      with an error naming the member. Other string types are unchanged.
    * C generator (also for plain C users): a quoted-string DEFAULT on a
      UTF8String, GeneralString, GraphicString, TeletexString, T61String,
      VideotexString, ObjectDescriptor, UTCTime or GeneralizedTime member now
      gets default_value_cmp / default_value_set, as for the other string
      types. The bytes of the literal are stored as written (UTF-8 for
      UTF8String). The generator does not check the syntax of a time literal;
      an invalid one is stored as is (decoding fills it in; the constraint
      check then rejects the value).
      Before, such a member had no callbacks: it was always encoded and was
      NULL when absent.

0.9.29-go.8:
    NEW:
    * Go backend: SET OF maps to []T like SEQUENCE OF (named or inline
      elements, top level, member, OPTIONAL member, CHOICE alternative,
      nested lists, SET OF a NULL type, extensible SIZE). Encode writes the
      elements in canonical order, so an unsorted slice comes back sorted from
      Decode. Before, a SET OF was refused with exit 70.
    * Go backend: SET maps to a struct like SEQUENCE (top level, member,
      OPTIONAL member, CHOICE alternative, inline, SET OF SET, DEFAULT
      members, extension additions and `[[ ]]` groups as Ext<N>). Encode
      writes the root members in canonical tag order (X.691 clause 21) and
      Decode reads them back, so the Go API shows textual order only. Before,
      a SET was refused with exit 70. An open-type (`&Value`) member of a
      SET is still refused (the C generator types it as ANY_t).
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): SET OF now has an APER encoder
      (SET_OF_encode_aper). The elements are sorted by their standalone APER
      encodings (X.691 22.1) and then encoded again, in that order, into the
      output, so alignment padding is right. Before, a SET OF PDU was
      rejected by `-oaper`.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): SET now supports UPER and APER
      (X.691 clause 21: canonical order of the root components). Generated
      asn_SET_specifics_t gained first_extension and ext_end (at the end, so
      older initializers still compile; regenerate to use PER on a SET).
    * Go backend: generated go.mod files now require rt v0.3.2; run
      `go mod tidy` once after regenerating. Not breaking: same module path,
      no Go API change. Code generated by go.8 needs v0.3.2 (the SET
      specifics fields and the zero-size arena slot).
    FIXES:
    * Go backend: encoding a zero-length BIT STRING (a plain, OPTIONAL or
      CHOICE-alternative member, or a SEQUENCE OF element) failed with
      "BIT STRING: value not given", so a value that Decode had produced
      could not be encoded again. The converter now always gives the C value
      a buffer. Every generated C converter that handles a BIT STRING
      changes, so regenerate.
    * Go backend: an OPTIONAL BIT STRING-alias member and an OPTIONAL inline
      SEQUENCE OF member of a type imported from another module no longer
      fail the build of the importing package (undefined: BitString /
      undefined: <List>). Their types are now package-qualified; a package
      without a BIT STRING of its own takes the helper type from a package
      it imports.
    * Go backend: a CHOICE alternative that is an empty `SEQUENCE {}` no
      longer panics in Encode (index out of range in the arena helper) or
      fails Decode with E_ALLOC. Every generated glue.go changes in the
      arena helper (allocStruct/allocPayload), so regenerate. The C runtime
      arena now serves a zero-size request as a distinct non-NULL slot.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): SET_OF_encode_uper used the sorted
      element buffers without checking for NULL (allocation or element
      encode failure) and went on to encode; it now fails the encode and
      frees the buffers on every path.
    * Go backend: SEQUENCE fields, CHOICE alternatives, type names and typed
      INTEGER value names that differ only by a hyphen before a digit
      (`a1` / `a-1`, `T1` / `T-1`) were refused as a name collision. The
      clashing name with `_<digit>` in its C name now keeps the underscore
      (`A1`, `A_1`), and every name built from it uses the same spelling:
      the inline type (`TA_1`), the CHOICE constant (`TPrA_1`), the element
      type of an inline SEQUENCE OF, the DEFAULT constant and the IE
      constructors. Names that do not clash are unchanged.
    * Go backend: ENUMERATED enumerators and named bits that differ only by a
      hyphen (`d1` / `d-1`) were refused as a name collision. Within one list
      the member with `_<digit>` in its C name now keeps the underscore
      (`DriftD1`, `DriftD_1`); lists without such a clash are unchanged.
      examples/rrc-7.1.0.asn1 gets past this.
    * C generator (also for plain C users): with -findirect-choice, a
      member or CHOICE alternative whose type is an alias of an alias
      (`PFL ::= Freq`) was declared `struct PFL *`, a struct that does not
      exist, so the member could not be assigned or dereferenced in C. The
      "struct X" spelling now names the constructed type the alias chain ends
      in (`struct Freq *`); `PFL_t` and other spellings are unchanged.
    * Go backend: a top-level alias of a CHOICE (`Alias ::= Orig`, also an
      alias of an alias) failed the cgo build: its converters used
      `Alias_PR` and `struct Alias__t2`, which C does not define (it has only
      `typedef Orig_t Alias_t;`). They now use the C names of the CHOICE the
      alias chain ends in (`Orig_PR`, `struct Orig__t2`). The Go types are
      unchanged; regenerate (asn1c -Fgo).
    * Go backend: a CHOICE alternative named after a C reserved word
      (`explicit`, `int`, `auto`, `default`, `struct`) failed the cgo build.
      asn1c upper-cases the first letter of such a union member (`Explicit`),
      but the converters wrote `choice.explicit`. They now use the upper-cased
      member and keep the lower-case `_PR` constant (`C_PR_explicit`). The Go
      names are unchanged; regenerate (asn1c -Fgo).
    * Go backend: a named SEQUENCE OF imported from another module
      (`l ItemList` with `IMPORTS ItemList FROM ModA`) generated
      `moda.moda.ItemList` in the importing package's glue.go, which does not
      compile (inside the owning package the same bug wrote a self-qualified
      name). The package qualifier is now taken off the field spelling before
      it is qualified for the package being emitted. Regenerate (asn1c -Fgo).
    * Go backend: a SEQUENCE with two or more inline CHOICE members failed
      the cgo build (`no new variables on left side of :=` or `cannot use
      *&v.P ... as TM value`): the glue declared the CHOICE value variable
      once per member at function scope. Each inline CHOICE now has its own
      block in the fill and size code. The generated code of specifications
      with one inline CHOICE changes only by the added braces; regenerate
      (asn1c -Fgo).
    * Go backend: a BIT STRING member, DEFAULT member or SEQUENCE OF BIT
      STRING imported from another module failed the cgo build
      (`cannot use v.Bm (variable of struct type moda.BitString) as BitString
      value`) when the importing module has a BIT STRING of its own. A
      BitString value is now spelled with its owning module's type and
      converted where the importing package's helpers take its own. Output
      for specifications without such an import is unchanged. The
      examples/rrc-7.1.0.asn1 build gets past this (SynchronisationParameters-r4).

0.9.29-go.7:
    NEW:
    * Go backend: all restricted character string types and
      UTCTime/GeneralizedTime map to Go `string`. BMPString and
      UniversalString are converted to and from UTF-8 (an unrepresentable
      string is an rt.ErrConstraint on Encode, an invalid C buffer an
      rt.ErrDecode on Decode); a DEFAULT on those two is refused.
    * Go backend: OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID map to []uint64 arcs
      everywhere. Encode returns rt.ErrConstraint for an arc above
      4294967295 (the C runtime holds 32 bits) or a value the runtime rejects.
    * Go backend: `[[ ]]` extension addition groups map to an optional nested
      struct `Ext<N> *<T>Ext<N>` (N numbered like the C backend's ext<N>); a
      nil group is absent on Encode and an absent group decodes to nil. It
      was a refusal before.
    * Go backend: a top-level plain NULL type (T ::= NULL) now gets the
      Encode / Decode API like every other PDU type; before, only
      `type T struct{}` was generated. Additive.

    FIXES:
    * Go backend: an empty PrintableString (T{P: ""}) no longer fails Encode
      with "value not given"; it is handled like the other restricted string
      types, in every position. Non-empty encodings are unchanged, and an
      empty value for a type with SIZE lower bound 1 is still a constraint
      error. Regenerate (asn1c -Fgo); no runtime change.
    * Go backend: SEQUENCE OF a NULL type (N ::= NULL, L ::= SEQUENCE OF N,
      also through an alias) was refused with "conv: unresolved seqof elem";
      it now maps to []N and round-trips the element count, at top level, as
      a member, OPTIONAL member and CHOICE alternative. A plain member of a
      NULL type (T ::= SEQUENCE { n N }) works too.
    * Go backend: names in an inline SEQUENCE or CHOICE alternative are no
      longer checked against the enclosing struct, so
      T ::= SEQUENCE { a SEQUENCE { x BOOLEAN }, x BOOLEAN } is no longer
      refused with "collision in module ...". The diagnostic path no longer
      repeats its last component.
    * C generator (also for plain C users): a type name defined in several
      modules (module-prefixed in C, e.g. ModA_Item) was spelled without the
      prefix in "struct X" forward declarations, OPTIONAL members, SEQUENCE
      OF elements and CHOICE alternatives, leaving an undefined struct in the
      headers (and Go output that did not compile). The prefix is now used.
    * C generator (also for plain C users): SEQUENCE OF / SET OF nested in
      another one with an inline SEQUENCE, SET or CHOICE inside
      (SEQUENCE OF SEQUENCE OF SEQUENCE { ... }) produced a header that did
      not compile; the inner typedef is now written first, so the generated
      text of such types changes (upstream asn1c issue 178).
    * C generator (also for plain C users): SEQUENCE OF / SET OF an inline
      INTEGER that needs its own descriptor (INTEGER (0..4294967295))
      referred to a descriptor that was never generated; it is now emitted.
    * Parser (also for plain C users): SEQUENCE (SIZE(..)) OF
      SEQUENCE (SIZE(..)) OF ... no longer aborts (exit 134), and a
      constraint trailing a list of lists (SEQUENCE OF SEQUENCE OF INTEGER
      (0..7)) now applies to the innermost element instead of failing with
      "Constraint type ValueRange is not applicable to SEQUENCE OF".
    * Go backend: the nested SEQUENCE OF shapes above and SEQUENCE OF an
      inline INTEGER (0..4294967295) now generate and round-trip against the
      C converter. SET OF is still refused by the Go backend.
    * Known limitation: a DEFAULT on a UTF8String, GeneralString,
      GraphicString, TeletexString, T61String, VideotexString,
      ObjectDescriptor, UTCTime or GeneralizedTime member is refused (the C
      generator supports DEFAULT only on IA5String, PrintableString,
      VisibleString and NumericString), though the message suggests otherwise
      (KNOWN-ISSUES.md #17).

0.9.29-go.6:
    NEW:
    * Go backend: SEQUENCE OF with an inline element type (INTEGER, BOOLEAN,
      OCTET STRING, BIT STRING, REAL, PrintableString, NULL, ENUMERATED,
      SEQUENCE, CHOICE, SEQUENCE OF) as a top-level type, member, OPTIONAL
      member or CHOICE alternative. Inline elements are named <Owner>Member.
    * Go backend: an anonymous SEQUENCE or CHOICE is supported as a SEQUENCE
      member (required or OPTIONAL), CHOICE alternative, nested, or inline
      SEQUENCE OF element.
    * Go backend: INTEGER members, OPTIONAL members, CHOICE alternatives and
      SEQUENCE OF elements whose range does not fit a C long use the same
      INTEGER_t <-> uint64/int64 conversion as a top-level type. A range
      fitting neither is refused with a clear message. (The C runtime's PER
      codec cannot encode values of INTEGER (0..2^64-1); Encode reports an
      error.)
    * Go backend: a CHOICE alternative named `present` is generated as the
      field PresentAlt (the discriminant Present and the constant
      <Choice>PrPresent are unchanged); it was a "collision" refusal before.

    FIXES:
    * Go backend: CRITICAL. Encode could panic with "asn1cgo: fixed-region
      undercounted by N" when a struct whose C size is not a multiple of 8
      (e.g. a SEQUENCE holding one ENUMERATED) is held through a pointer
      (OPTIONAL member, CHOICE alternative under -findirect-choice, OPTIONAL
      reference) or is an element of a SEQUENCE OF with an odd item count,
      and more allocations follow. go.1 to go.5 are affected. Regenerate
      with the fixed asn1c; no runtime change is needed.
    * Go backend: extension additions without OPTIONAL
      (`SEQUENCE { a ..., ..., b BOOLEAN }`) generated Go that did not
      compile. Extension additions are now always pointers, like the C
      struct members; a nil addition encodes as absent. Not breaking; an
      addition with a DEFAULT stays a plain value.
    * Docs: added libasn1compiler_go/KNOWN-ISSUES.md, listing the known bugs
      and limitations of the Go backend.

0.9.29-go.5:
    NEW:
    * Go backend: named-bit BIT STRING (`BIT STRING { a(0), b(1) }`) is
      supported. The value is the plain BitString and each named bit becomes
      an int bit-position constant <Type><Bit> (<Parent><Member> for an
      inline member, <Choice><Alt> for a CHOICE alternative). Still refused:
      a DEFAULT on a named-bit type, and SEQUENCE OF an inline named-bit
      BIT STRING.
    * Go backend: generated go.mod files require rt v0.3.1; run
      `go mod tidy` once after regenerating. Not breaking.

    FIXES:
    * Go backend: CRITICAL. Encoding a present inline OPTIONAL BIT STRING
      member crashed (SIGSEGV) or failed with a constraint error: the BIT
      STRING record was written into the pointer slot. go.1 to go.4 are
      affected. Regenerate with the fixed asn1c; no runtime change is needed.
    * Go backend / C runtime (also for plain C users): no more
      `"_REENTRANT" redefined` cgo warning; the feature macros in
      GeneralizedTime.c and REAL.c are #ifndef-guarded, in skeletons/ and the
      Go runtime alike (rt v0.3.1). New tests/run-rt-skeleton-sync.sh checks
      that both copies match and the runtime compiles with -Werror=cpp.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): NativeEnumerated_encode_aper stores
      the bsearch result as const (fixes -Wdiscarded-qualifiers). Ships in
      rt v0.3.1.
    * Go backend: several modules that each own BIT STRING members in one
      -Fgo run now build; a module's helpers use its own BitString instead of
      the first module's.
    * Go backend: an OPTIONAL member whose type is a BIT STRING type
      (`ref Ranged OPTIONAL`, also named-bit and imported) generated code
      that did not compile.

0.9.29-go.4:
    FIXES:
    * Go backend: BREAKING. The runtime module is renamed to
      github.com/Frozen-Potato/asn1c/libasn1compiler_go/rt/go, v0.3.0;
      regenerate. Generated go.mod fetches it (run `go mod tidy` once);
      ASN1CGO_RT_LOCAL=<dir> selects a local checkout via replace/go.work.
      ASN1CGO_GO_MODULE_PREFIX no longer applies to the runtime. `make
      install` ships the rt C files in <pkgdatadir>/go-rt.
    * Go backend: DEFAULT members are supported. A member with a DEFAULT is a
      plain value T (not a pointer) with a <Type><Field>Default constant.
      Supported: BOOLEAN / INTEGER / ENUMERATED values, PrintableString
      quoted strings, OCTET STRING and BIT STRING (no named bits) 'H / 'B
      values. Other forms are rejected before the C pass (exit 70), leaving
      -D untouched.
    * Go backend: CHOICE extension index >= 64 is no longer refused.
    * C generator: negative INTEGER DEFAULT values get valid C names and
      INT64_MIN a valid literal; OCTET STRING / BIT STRING hstring/bstring
      DEFAULTs now get comparison/set callbacks; 'HH printable value fixed.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): the APER SEQUENCE encoder dropped
      DEFAULT members and the APER decoder filled extension defaults from
      the wrong table; both fixed.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): PER normally-small length and
      number >= 64 fixed in APER and UPER (SEQUENCE with > 64 extension
      additions, CHOICE extension index, ENUMERATED extension value);
      encodings of such values change.
    * C runtime (also for plain C users): extension additions equal to their
      DEFAULT are omitted in PER (canonical form).
    * C runtime: fix a leak of the extension presence bitmap on an error
      path.
    * asn1c: false positives for synthesized open-type names removed from
      the name-clash check.
    * BREAKING: a real name clash under -fcompound-names now fails the run
      (non-zero exit) instead of only warning.
    * Go backend: -Fgo basenames that collide with the Go standard library
      are rejected unless ASN1CGO_GO_MODULE_PREFIX is set.

0.9.29-go.3:
    FIXES:
    * Go backend: requires rt v0.2.3; regenerate and republish the Go tree
      and runtime together.
    * Go backend: generated go.mod/go.work minimum Go version lowered from
      1.27.1 to 1.21.0; existing go.work files keep their go line.
    * Go backend: APER decode runs asn1c's C stack guard
      (ASN1CGO_C_STACK_MAX, default 96 KiB, override with
      -DASN1CGO_C_STACK_MAX=<bytes>). Very deeply nested input that could
      crash the process is rejected with ErrDecode; trees within the budget
      but deeper than 64 units still get ErrDepth.
    * Go backend: Encode returns ErrAlloc on out-of-memory or block-size
      overflow instead of aborting the process.
    * Go backend: unsupported constructs (DEFAULT, [[ ]], unsupported types,
      CHOICE extension index >= 64, invalid -Fgo basename or
      ASN1CGO_GO_MODULE_PREFIX) are rejected before the C pass, so a rejected
      spec leaves -D untouched; a Go failure after the C pass says that -D was
      updated but the Go tree was not.
    * Go backend: concurrent generators sharing a parent directory are
      serialised with flock on <parent>/.go.work.lock, so no go.work `use`
      entry is lost (advisory; local filesystems).
    * asn1fix: fix strict-aliasing undefined behaviour in the extension list
      handling that made asn1c crash (SIGSEGV) on some specifications with
      gcc 16 at -O2.
    * Tests: new tests/run-gowork-race.sh.

0.9.29-go.2:
    FIXES:
    * APER (also for plain C users): CHOICE and ENUMERATED extension index is
      encoded/decoded as a normally small non-negative whole number (X.691
      #10.6); the wire encoding of extension alternatives/values changes.
    * Go backend: requires rt v0.2.2.
    * Go backend: -Fgo output is all-or-nothing (staging dir + atomic swap),
      go.work is updated atomically, every failure is printed.
    * Go backend: fix named BOOLEAN typedef conversion.
    * Go backend: unknown IOC id reported as IOC_UNKNOWN; error codes
      documented.
    * Go backend: SEQUENCE OF elements are cast to the callee's parameter
      type in the generated *_from_tree code.

0.9.29-go.1:
    FEATURES:
    * Go backend: -Fgo=<dir> generates Go types and APER Encode/Decode via
      cgo (libasn1compiler_go, runtime rt v0.2.1).

    FIXES:
    * APER (also for plain C users): fix CHOICE extension index encoding for
      extensible types.
    * PER (also for plain C users): fix SEQUENCE with length greater than
      65535.
    * APER (also for plain C users): fix the X.691 #16.11 condition and
      16K-fragment handling (zero-length terminator after a full final
      fragment) in OCTET STRING and open type encoding/decoding; boundary
      checks and variable initializations hardened in the decoder.


0.9.??:
    FEATURES:
    * Added support for basic Information Object Sets driven code generation.
    * Added OER support.
    * Added LTE RRC example (Bi-Ruei, Chiu).
    * Added IEEE 1609.2 example.
    * Added SAE J2735 example.

    NOTABLE:
    * Converter example (included by default):
      * converter-sample.c renamed into converter-example.c
      * make converter-example.mk file for building that converter
      * asn1c -no-gen-example to stop generating converter-example.{c,mk}
    * asn1c -no-gen-example option to disable converter-example generation.
    * Added random value generation (-R option to converter-example).
    * Added LibFuzzer-based randomized tests for supported transfer syntaxes
      (DER, OER, UPER, XER) into tests/tests-randomized. See the following
      article to get the latest LibFuzzer-enabled clang on macOS:
        https://medium.com/@levwalkin/compile-llvm-clang-libfuzzer-b61e82718430
      then ensure the new clang is in the way:
        CC=clang CXX=clang++ ./configure --enable-Werror --enable-test-fuzzer
    * OBJECT IDENTIFIER and RELATIVE-OID API simplified.
    * uper_encode() API got new argument (breaks API compatibility).
    * asn1c -gen-XXX flags are deprecated. Use -no-gen-XXX to disable codecs.

    FIXES:
    * CVE-2017-12966 verified not present.
    * Fix incomplete (failed) CHOICE XER decoding memory leak.
      (Severity: medium; Security impact: medium)
    * Fix REAL type overwrite conversion memory leak.
      (Severity: low; Security impact: medium)
    * Fix UPER string decoding constrained only by lower bound > 0
      (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
    * Fix UPER decoding of large [bit-]strings of size a multiple of 16K
      (Severity: low; Security impact: none)
    * Fix XER decoder crash on maliciously constructed ENUMERATED input.
      (Severity: medium; Security impact: medium)

